/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Fuzzing artefacts. Seed corpora ARE committed (docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md §3); crash
# artefacts are not — a crash gets a regression test and a sanitised corpus entry instead.
#
# Leading `**/` matters: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory,
# so a bare `fuzz/target` would only match one at the repository root. The fuzz crate lives at
# crates/strypt-core/fuzz/, per docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §2.
**/fuzz/target/
**/fuzz/artifacts/
**/fuzz/coverage/
# libFuzzer's working corpus, which reaches thousands of machine-generated files within
# minutes. The curated seeds are committed separately, under fuzz/seeds/.
**/fuzz/corpus/

# Never commit real user files. Test fixtures must contain no real personal data
# (CONTRIBUTING.md); scratch files must not leak into history.
/scratch
*.local

# Bytecode from the fixture generators. `make_png_fixtures.py` imports the JPEG tool for its
# shared TIFF builder, which is what creates this directory.
__pycache__/

.DS_Store
# Codex's local tooling, kept out of the repository by choice (2026-08-19).
#
# Note the asymmetry, because it is deliberate rather than an oversight: `.claude/` IS tracked,
# since CLAUDE.md §6 points at `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/hooks/` as the early local
# warning for the ADR-0004 and ADR-0007 gates. `.codex/hooks/` mirrors those same two gates and
# AGENTS.md mirrors the working agreement — so anyone relying on either is relying on an
# untracked local copy that no other clone has and that nothing keeps in step with CLAUDE.md.
# `.codex/hooks.json` also hardcodes absolute paths, so it is not portable as written.
.codex/
AGENTS.md

# The real-producer corpus (docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 1, exit criterion 1).
#
# These rules live here rather than in a nested `.gitignore` so that every ignore rule in this
# repository has one home and one place to read the reasoning for it.
#
# `.cache/` holds re-clonable upstream sample repositories — large, somebody else's history,
# and `build_real_corpus.py` fetches them again on demand.
/real-producer-corpus/.cache/
#
# The fixtures themselves stay out of history too. The reasons have changed, so read them
# again before assuming this rule still rests on what it originally did.
#
# ORIGINALLY, and no longer: real personal data. A sweep on 2026-08-20 found four real names
# in Canon MakerNote OwnerName fields, two more in PDF Author fields, a device serial number,
# and live GPS coordinates for five photographs — Helsinki, Hämeenlinna, Kansas City and
# Madrid. **`sanitise_corpus.py` now replaces all of it with synthetic values on every build**,
# verified, with the build aborting rather than writing a manifest if any real value survives.
# So `docs/TESTING_STRATEGY.md` §3's first rule no longer blocks committing these files.
#
# STILL STANDING, and why the rule remains:
#
#   1. Size. §3's second rule — large fixtures belong in a fetched-on-demand corpus, not in
#      git history forever — applies at 32 MB regardless of what the files contain.
#   2. Licensing, which is unresolved. `SOURCES.md` pins down exactly one of three upstreams
#      (py-pdf/sample-files, CC-BY-SA-4.0 — copyleft, which would put share-alike assets in an
#      MIT-OR-Apache-2.0 tree). ianare/exif-samples says "upstream licensing applies" and
#      imazen/codec-corpus says "see per-dataset licenses". Redistributing 91 files of
#      undetermined licence is a separate problem from redistributing personal data, and
#      sanitising fixed only the latter.
#
# Committing the corpus therefore needs the licensing question answered first, and probably a
# curated subset rather than all 32 MB.
#
# Nothing is lost by this. `build_real_corpus.py` reproduces all 101 fixtures into these exact
# directories, verified byte-identical on rebuild, so the corpus is a command away for anyone
# who wants it. What is committed is the recipe and the manifests: enough to know precisely
# what was tested and to reproduce it, without the payload.
/real-producer-corpus/real-corpus/jpeg/
/real-producer-corpus/real-corpus/pdf/
/real-producer-corpus/real-corpus/png/
/real-producer-corpus/real-corpus/webp/
/real-producer-corpus/real-corpus/generated/

# Loose Python bytecode outside a __pycache__ directory.
*.py[cod]
